## Session summary — criteria NOT met, but the ROOT CAUSE was found

After 37 prior sessions of dir-block cache-coherency heuristics that never converged, this session **moved the root of the 8/tcp `dir_reuse_coherency` single-dirent loss to the DLM grant layer** with decisive instrumentation.

**The decisive measurement:** The genuine loss is a node's xfsaild **background-reflushing dir block 0** (`buf_cnt=N` over durable `disk_cnt=N+1`), and at that write the buffer reads `bufgen==dirgen` **AND** `buf_epoch==master_ep` (e.g. 329==329) — **fully "current" by both the gen token and the node's own held grant dir-epoch, yet content-stale.** The node retained a **stale EX grant** across a peer's EX-modify. This explains why every gen/epoch read-side heuristic failed: **the freshness tokens lie** — the node believes it still owns the tenure under which the buffer was stamped. Corroborated by `P-STALEMASTER-GRANT` firing (transient **split-brain mastership** — two nodes briefly master the same resource under the 8-node storm and grant concurrent EX, which the per-master double-grant check can't see), with `P-DOUBLEGRANT`=0×.

**Refuted with evidence (all reverted to default-off):** write-side `dir_subset_guard` (shutdown), my `dir_release_retire_done` (shutdown), `dir_tenure_evict=1` (best read-side: 0%→~67%, but insufficient — buffer epoch == held grant epoch), `dir_tenure_stale_bypass` (loss + shutdowns). Also proved the release flush already retires all in_ail buffers (`P38-POSTREL-ZOMBIE`=0×), so it is *not* a zombie-survives-release bug.

**The fix (GPT-5.5 consult #2, full design saved):** DLM must guarantee one-master-per-resource-generation + no-EX-grant-until-old-holder-drained-or-fenced, and the FS must enforce no-metadata-writeback-without-a-current-EX-write-authority-token. Smallest piece to try first: a per-resource write-authority token that xfsaild must hold before submitting a dir-metadata write (drops a clean stale buffer instead of writing it) — then the membership recovery-barrier / stale-grant rejection. Must guard the passing 1/2/4 tcp against regression.

Everything is captured in memory (`sess38-DECISIVE-loss-is-stale-EX-grant-bufepoch-eq-masterep`, `sess38-GPT2-DLM-fix-design-...`, `sess38-HEAD-handoff`). Criteria are not met, so I have not written the marker — the loop continues with the root cause and a concrete DLM fix plan for the next session.

